course: dictionary
lesson: 8599
title: A Scot and scot-free
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Scot is a person from Scotland, one of the four nations of the United Kingdom. «Ye're fine, stop greetin'» is in Scots, a language closely related to English. You can work out that greetin' means crying from the clues around it: Callie has been hurt at school, and her mam tells her to stop and goes back to her phone.
explain: Scots words are not spelling mistakes. «Dinnae» is Scots for don't, and «ken» means know. When you meet one, read the words around it, then swap in your own meaning to check it still makes sense.
explain: Scot also appears in the phrase scot-free, which means without being punished or harmed. This has nothing to do with Scotland. Long ago, a scot was a tax or payment, so to get off scot-free was to escape paying it.
fact: A Scot is a person from Scotland.
fact: The Scots were a people from Ireland who settled in western Scotland about 1,500 years ago, and they gave Scotland its name.
fact: Scots, Scottish and Scotch are related words, and Scots is also the name of a language.
fact: In Scots, «dinnae» means don't, and «ken» means know.
fact: «Scot-free» means without being punished or harmed, and it has nothing to do with Scotland.
exercise: In Scots, «Ye're fine, stop greetin'» means greetin' is what? | Laughing | Running | Sleeping | *Crying
exercise: What is a Scot? | *A person from Scotland | A person from Wales | A kind of cold weather
exercise: Dad says «Dinnae worry». What does dinnae mean? | Dance | Dinosaur | Dinner | *Don't
test: Lee broke a window and got off scot-free. What does scot-free mean? | Scottish and proud | Running very fast | *Without being punished | Very wet and muddy
test: In Scots, «ken» means what? | *Know | Kind | Kick | Kiss
exam: Which statement about the word scot in scot-free is true? | It means happy and relaxed | *It has nothing to do with Scotland, because an old scot was a tax | It means a person from Scotland | It is the name of a Scottish dish
